bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_space_layoutunit_tie_2026-11-27, 0, "Chrome 159, 400px div, Arial 16px: <span class=b style=margin-right:0.6px> (100px inline-block) then ' <span class=z></span> <span class=b>' puts the last box at 110 (100.59375 + 2 x 285/64 = 109.5, rounded up). Simple gives 109: it carries each space as 4.445 px. 0.7px (110) and 0.4px (109) match. Fix needs LayoutUnit (1/64) text advances in the inline pen carry. Pinned as an open gap in test/01_unit/browser_engine/inline_line_end_space_align_chrome159_spec.spl (AC-20 table)."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_space_layoutunit_tie_2026-11-27, P3, open, "web render: a space advance is carried as its exact width (4.445 px), not Chrome's LayoutUnit (285/64 = 4.453), so a 109.5 tie rounds the wrong way", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl, 5122, test/01_unit/browser_engine/inline_line_end_space_align_chrome159_spec.spl, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

